        {
          "id": 1998610421,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hm.  I don't see any built-in way to have `g_ptr_array_foreach` bail out part-way through the iteration; We'd have to have some member inside `user_data` indicate that further iterations can bail out without doing any processing.\n\nReally the goal of my prior change was to separate out the _policy_ (selection of which `open_info`s to try, and in what order) from the evaluation of the policy (the part which was replicated six times)... with that accomplished (modulo an error in a `sizeof` expression), a better next step might be to refactor further such that the whole pointer-array thing becomes unnecessary.  I have a draft of just such a change in progress and I'll get back to it tomorrow.\n\nFor the time being, I'll set this to \"draft\" and it can stay in the queue.\n\nThanks -- as always -- for the feedback!",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
